system "Background job"

# A job is retried until it succeeds or runs out of attempts. Either way it
# must reach a final status: nothing may be left "running" forever.

state
  status is one of queued, running, succeeded, failed
  attempts is an integer from 0 to 3

initially
  status is queued
  attempts is 0

always
  status is failed implies attempts is 3

sometimes
  status is succeeded
  status is failed

eventually
  status is succeeded or status is failed

whenever status is running eventually status is not running

terminal when status is succeeded or status is failed

fair action start
  requires status is queued
  status becomes running
  attempts becomes attempts + 1

action succeed
  requires status is running
  status becomes succeeded

action crash
  requires status is running
  status becomes if attempts is 3 then failed else queued

scenario "Third time lucky"
  start
  crash
  start
  crash
  start
  succeed
  expect status is succeeded and attempts is 3

scenario "Out of attempts"
  start
  crash
  start
  crash
  start
  crash
  expect status is failed
  reject start
  reject succeed
  reject crash
